{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Moses arose, and Joshua his minister.</b> I do not know what Joshua's role is here, and I say that the disciple escorts the master up to the boundary of the mountain's perimeter, beyond which he is not permitted to go. From there וַיַּעַל מֹשֶׁה לְבַדּוֹ אֶל הַר הָאֱלֹהִים — and Joshua pitched his tent there and stayed there all forty days. For so we find: when Moses came down, וַיִּשְׁמַע יְהוֹשֻׁעַ אֶת קוֹל הָעָם בְּרֵעֹה (Exodus 32:17) — we learn that Joshua was not among them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:18.708653299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}